# Python Backend

- Type hints everywhere, Pydantic for all schemas
- Async functions for all API endpoints
- Service layer: routes → services → database (no business logic in handlers)
- Dependency injection via `Depends()`
- All queries scoped by `organization_id` (multi-tenancy)
- Alembic for all schema changes
- LLM prompts in `backend/app/prompts/` as Jinja2 — never hardcode
- All LLM outputs parsed into Pydantic models
- Every state change creates an `AuditEntry`

```python
# ❌ BAD — business logic in route
@router.post("")
async def create(data: CreateSchema, db: DbSession):
    result = SomeModel(**data.model_dump())
    db.add(result)
    return result

# ✅ GOOD — route delegates to service, scoped by org
@router.post("")
async def create(data: CreateSchema, db: DbSession, org_id: OrganizationId):
    return await some_service.create(db, org_id, data)
```
